Wait, that is wrong. Here is the correct transcription:

<page type="text">
  <layout>One printed page, single centred column of text. A decorative ornament rule stands at the top. No margin notes, no running head, no page number.</layout>
  <main_text>
    <p type="ornament">[ornament rule]</p>
    <head level="2"><i>Amplissimis, genere &amp; virtute conspicuis Viris ac Dominis,</i></head>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> ANTHONIO à GRAFFENRIED, Inclytæ Reipublicæ Bernensis Consuli dignissimo, gravissimo, ac susceptori suo è Sacro fonte æternùm colendo.</p>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> JOH. RODOLPHO WURSTENBERGERO, ejusdem Reip. Tribuno plebis spectatissimo, affini suo plurimùm honorando.</p>
    <head level="2">Ut Et</head>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> DAVIDI ALBINO, Philosophiæ Professori acutissimo, Collegij minoris inspectori fidelissimo, hospiti suo amantissimo.</p>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> PETRO MALACRIDÆ, Ecclesiæ, quæ colligitur in Wyl, Pastori vigilantissimo, olim hospiti suo admodùm colendo.</p>
    <head level="2">Quin Etiam</head>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> SIGISMUNDO à WATTENWYL, Præfecturâ in Morsee laudabiliter defuncto, patruo suo omni honore prosequendo.</p>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> ALBERTO à WATTENWYL, Chiliarchæ in Galliâ strenuissimè defuncto, patrueli suo plurimùm observando.</p>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> DANIELI STÜRLERO, Gubernatori in Bomon meritissimo, Affini suo ad aras usq; colendo.</p>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> SAMUELI à WATTENWYL, Præfecto in Romamonstier dignissimo, Agnato ac Tutori suo observandissimo, fidelissimo.</p>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> JACOBO à WATTENWYL, Chiliarchæ in patriâ animosissimo, Fratri suo omni φιλαδελφία prosequendo.</p>
    <p><i>Dn.</i> NICOLAO à WATTENWYL, Inclytæ Reip. Bernensis ducentûm-viro meritissimo, patrueli suo plurimùm observando.</p>
    <p><i>Has disquisitiones philosophicas sacras facit</i></p>
    <p>Joh. Anthonius à Wattenwyl, Resp.</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The Greek word in the list is φιλαδελφία as printed. Ornament rule at top is decorative only. Faint show-through text near the bottom is not transcribed.</notes>
</page>